    ❯❱ rules.untrusted-retrieval-into-prompt
          ❰❰ Blocking ❱❱
          Text returned from a retrieval/RAG lookup is concatenated into an LLM message body without going   
          through a delimiting, escaping, or provenance-tagging step first. Retrieved documents are attacker-
          reachable in most RAG deployments (anyone who can get content into the corpus, or compromise a     
          source the corpus indexes, controls this text). Mixed untagged into the same message the model     
          treats as instructions, this is the classic indirect prompt injection setup: the model has no      
          structural signal that this text is "reference data" rather than "things to obey." Wrap retrieved  
          content in an explicit, consistently-applied delimiter or data-marking scheme (OWASP LLM01:2026    
          mitigation #6) and keep it out of the instruction channel, or treat it as untrusted input and re-  
          validate any instruction-like content it contains before use.                                      
                                                                                                             
